{/*
  The two-planes diagram — the second of the five-diagram family, conforming to the shared
  legend and rendering contract (docs/design/docs-site-visual-blueprint.md §5): hand-authored
  theme-aware inline SVG, colors only from the bound token custom properties
  (--perk-* / --sl-color-*), operational labels IBM Plex Mono 500 at >= 16 CSS px,
  annotations Inter, no animation, nothing hover-only.

  One <figure class="perk-diagram"> wraps two fully-labeled <svg role="img"> variants
  (data-variant="wide" horizontal, data-variant="narrow" stacked vertical, same reading
  order); the scoped @container query on the figure's inline size (compositions.css makes
  figure.perk-diagram an inline-size container) display:none's exactly one at any width —
  narrow by default, wide only where the content column fits its 736-unit viewBox at scale 1,
  so every label renders at its declared ≥16px size — removing it from rendering AND the
  accessibility tree so a single accessible image is exposed. Browsers without container-query
  support keep the content-identical narrow variant. Each variant carries its own <title> +
  <desc> associated via aria-labelledby (document-unique ids).

  The two plane/ownership regions (10px-rounded containers) flank the durable-state artifact
  shape (document-tab: var(--sl-color-accent-low) fill + border) whose contents are the
  genuinely durable/canonical artifacts — plans and objectives (GitHub issues; on Linear,
  plan issues and objective projects), pull requests, and pushed branch commits. The plan ref (.perk/workflow/plan-ref.json) is a
  gitignored, regenerable local mirror (shared/contracts.md) and stays OUT of this shape.
  Solid bidirectional arrows carry the exchanged-artifact labels.

  Deliberately static and prop-free: a malformed component fails `astro build`, and the
  post-build structural checks (docs/site/checks/built-site.test.mjs) cover the output.
*/}

<figure class="perk-diagram">
  <svg
    role="img"
    data-variant="wide"
    viewBox="0 0 736 208"
    aria-labelledby="perk-planes-wide-title perk-planes-wide-desc"
  >
    <title id="perk-planes-wide-title">Two planes around one durable state</title>
    <desc id="perk-planes-wide-desc">
      Two plane regions — Exterior, the perk CLI (scaffolding, worktrees, launching Pi), and
      Interior, the Pi session (stages, doors, tools) — flank a central durable-state
      artifact holding plans and objectives (GitHub issues; on Linear, plan issues and
      objective projects), pull requests, and pushed branch commits. A solid bidirectional arrow labeled "plan issues · branches"
      joins Exterior and durable state; a solid bidirectional arrow labeled "plan issues ·
      pull requests" joins durable state and Interior. The planes exchange nothing directly.
    </desc>
    <g>
      <rect class="plane" x="2" y="8" width="210" height="160" rx="10" />
      <text class="region-heading" x="20" y="38">Exterior</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="20" y="70">the perk CLI</text>
      <text class="annotation muted" x="20" y="98">scaffolding · worktrees</text>
      <text class="annotation muted" x="20" y="126">launching Pi</text>

      <line class="exchange" x1="220" y1="88" x2="254" y2="88" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="220,84.5 220,91.5 214,88" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="254,84.5 254,91.5 260,88" />
      <text class="exchange-label" x="237" y="196">plan issues · branches</text>

      <rect class="artifact" x="262" y="8" width="64" height="26" rx="6" />
      <rect class="artifact" x="262" y="20" width="212" height="140" rx="6" />
      <text class="region-heading" x="278" y="50">Durable state</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="278" y="80">plans &amp; objectives</text>
      <text class="annotation muted" x="278" y="104">(GitHub / Linear)</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="278" y="128">pull requests</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="278" y="152">pushed branch commits</text>

      <line class="exchange" x1="482" y1="88" x2="516" y2="88" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="482,84.5 482,91.5 476,88" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="516,84.5 516,91.5 522,88" />
      <text class="exchange-label" x="499" y="196">plan issues · pull requests</text>

      <rect class="plane" x="524" y="8" width="210" height="160" rx="10" />
      <text class="region-heading" x="542" y="38">Interior</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="542" y="70">the Pi session</text>
      <text class="annotation muted" x="542" y="98">stages · doors · tools</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <svg
    role="img"
    data-variant="narrow"
    viewBox="0 0 288 496"
    aria-labelledby="perk-planes-narrow-title perk-planes-narrow-desc"
  >
    <title id="perk-planes-narrow-title">Two planes around one durable state (stacked)</title>
    <desc id="perk-planes-narrow-desc">
      Stacked top to bottom: the Exterior plane region — the perk CLI (scaffolding,
      worktrees, launching Pi) — a solid bidirectional arrow labeled "plan issues ·
      branches", the central durable-state artifact holding plans and objectives (GitHub
      issues; on Linear, plan issues and objective projects), pull requests, and pushed
      branch commits, a solid bidirectional
      arrow labeled "plan issues · pull requests", then the Interior plane region — the Pi
      session (stages, doors, tools). The planes exchange nothing directly.
    </desc>
    <g>
      <rect class="plane" x="2" y="4" width="284" height="128" rx="10" />
      <text class="region-heading" x="20" y="32">Exterior</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="20" y="62">the perk CLI</text>
      <text class="annotation muted" x="20" y="88">scaffolding · worktrees</text>
      <text class="annotation muted" x="20" y="114">launching Pi</text>

      <line class="exchange" x1="39" y1="144" x2="39" y2="170" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="35.5,144 42.5,144 39,138" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="35.5,170 42.5,170 39,176" />
      <text class="exchange-label side" x="60" y="162">plan issues · branches</text>

      <rect class="artifact" x="2" y="182" width="64" height="26" rx="6" />
      <rect class="artifact" x="2" y="194" width="284" height="140" rx="6" />
      <text class="region-heading" x="20" y="224">Durable state</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="20" y="254">plans &amp; objectives</text>
      <text class="annotation muted" x="20" y="278">(GitHub / Linear)</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="20" y="302">pull requests</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="20" y="326">pushed branch commits</text>

      <line class="exchange" x1="39" y1="346" x2="39" y2="372" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="35.5,346 42.5,346 39,340" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="35.5,372 42.5,372 39,378" />
      <text class="exchange-label side" x="60" y="364">plan issues · pull requests</text>

      <rect class="plane" x="2" y="384" width="284" height="106" rx="10" />
      <text class="region-heading" x="20" y="412">Interior</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="20" y="442">the Pi session</text>
      <text class="annotation muted" x="20" y="468">stages · doors · tools</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
</figure>

<style>
  svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  svg[data-variant="wide"] {
    max-width: 736px;
    display: none;
  }
  svg[data-variant="narrow"] {
    max-width: 288px;
  }
  @container (min-width: 736px) {
    svg[data-variant="wide"] {
      display: block;
    }
    svg[data-variant="narrow"] {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  .plane {
    fill: var(--perk-surface);
    stroke: var(--perk-border);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .artifact {
    fill: var(--sl-color-accent-low);
    stroke: var(--perk-border);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .region-heading {
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 500;
    fill: var(--perk-text);
  }
  .annotation {
    font-family: var(--sl-font), sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    fill: var(--perk-text);
  }
  .annotation.muted {
    fill: var(--perk-muted);
  }
  /* U19 (§12) — light finish: exchange-line presence next to the elevated cards. */
  .exchange {
    stroke: var(--perk-muted);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    fill: none;
  }
  .arrowhead {
    fill: var(--perk-muted);
  }
  .exchange-label {
    font-family: var(--sl-font), sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    fill: var(--perk-muted);
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .exchange-label.side {
    text-anchor: start;
  }
</style>
